Daniel, I think you were there watching that talk with me.

00:46:08.243 --> 00:46:09.043
It was so good.

00:46:09.043 --> 00:46:10.163
We had such a fun time.

00:46:10.163 --> 00:46:11.603
Okay, fantastic.

00:46:12.642 --> 00:46:15.762
Can we get in one more question in our last five minutes?

00:46:15.762 --> 00:46:18.322
Because I would love to ask you for a piece of career advice.

00:46:18.322 --> 00:46:19.442
Maybe we can even get into.

00:46:21.603 --> 00:46:27.682
Yeah, I think one thing I've done really useful in my career is just like making connections

00:46:27.682 --> 00:46:31.442
in your organization to people who work in a very different area to you.

00:46:32.322 --> 00:46:37.522
I've always found it really helpful for like learning about the organization

00:46:37.603 --> 00:46:41.922
and things about the data that you're working with.

00:46:41.922 --> 00:46:46.562
And they'll often have knowledge about a data set that I didn't even know existed

00:46:46.562 --> 00:46:49.282
or how something was done in the past.

00:46:49.282 --> 00:46:51.202
And that's always really useful.

00:46:52.082 --> 00:46:53.603
It pays to be in person.

00:46:53.603 --> 00:46:55.603
I feel like much easier to do in person.

00:46:55.603 --> 00:46:59.763
Bring food in was always a way to just draw people and you could meet a lot of people.

00:46:59.763 --> 00:47:00.883
But it's definitely harder.

00:47:00.883 --> 00:47:05.682
I work remote now based in Seattle, but we're working remotely for Washington.

00:47:06.243 --> 00:47:08.562
And so figuring out how to do that.

00:47:08.562 --> 00:47:13.682
I think like just scheduling kind of those like more informal coffee chats,

00:47:13.682 --> 00:47:15.763
virtual coffee chats has been really helpful.

00:47:16.963 --> 00:47:19.603
When there's a chance to be in person, I like go in every once in a while

00:47:19.603 --> 00:47:21.603
and I'll tell everyone and try and get them to come.

00:47:22.322 --> 00:47:25.763
And then finding those people in your organization who seem to know everyone

00:47:25.763 --> 00:47:28.883
and taking advantage of that because they will be able to introduce you

00:47:29.603 --> 00:47:30.723
to people that are very helpful.

00:47:31.523 --> 00:47:33.442
These are fantastic suggestions.

00:47:33.442 --> 00:47:34.243
I love that.

00:47:34.562 --> 00:47:35.763
Go find somebody.

00:47:35.763 --> 00:47:41.042
Go find their Rachel at an organization who's been there for a million years

00:47:41.042 --> 00:47:44.802
and knows all the people and is going to be fully open to just like

00:47:44.802 --> 00:47:46.643
introducing you to everybody.

00:47:46.643 --> 00:47:48.003
And now I get to do that too.

00:47:48.003 --> 00:47:49.363
New people will message me and I'll be like,

00:47:49.363 --> 00:47:50.162
have you met this person?

00:47:50.162 --> 00:47:50.963
Have you met this person?

00:47:50.963 --> 00:47:51.763
Have you met this person?

00:47:52.322 --> 00:47:55.763
I will be more than happy to invite you to talk to everybody.

00:47:55.763 --> 00:47:59.843
But yes, when you can go have coffee chats, do all that stuff.

00:47:59.843 --> 00:48:00.402
Fantastic.

